WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.540
Sony's standalone Venom movie has come and
gone, and we all survived.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.440
Now let's eat some lobsters and try to explain
the end of Venom.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.360
Major spoilers ahead.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.620
Switching sides

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.980
By the movie's climax, the goopy alien Venom
tells Eddie Brock that he's ready to help

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.400
humanity repel his race's invasion of Earth.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.180
Why?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.040
According to the alien, it's because on his
home planet, he's kind of a loser, just like

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:21.540
Brock.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.260
It's a great line, but it doesn't really explain
the pivotal moment.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.560
However, it could have some roots in the comics.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:33.120
In Venom: First Host #1, we learn that the
symbiote that would eventually become Venom

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.870
was cast out from the rest of its gloopy brothers
and sisters, possibly the result of some kind

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.760
of "cognitive damage."

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.280
As a result, Venom's never really been quite
like the rest of the Marvel Comics symbiotes

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:43.820
we've met.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.420
Of course, none of that sounds as good as
Venom calling himself a loser, so it didn't

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.380
make it into the script.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.180
Alien Nation

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.680
Life Foundation head honcho Carlton Drake
was up to his armpits in symbiotes for most

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.540
of the movie, but by the end, only Riot and
Venom remained.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.440
So, you may be wondering: what happened to
the rest?

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.400
Well apparently the symbiotes couldn't live
in their given hosts and died...which kind

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.520
of makes Riot's plan to steal a rocket and
bring a whole bunch more anaerobic symbiotes

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.600
to an oxygen-rich planet filled with incompatible
hosts kind of...dumb.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.119
"You suck."

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:15.960
But enough about all that!

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.320
Did you see the part where Venom chomped on
some guy's head?

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.380
That was great.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.100
That red-haired Bozo?

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.600
So what's the deal with Woody Harrelson and
that bright red wig during the first post-credits

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.100
scene?

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.760
Well that, dear friends, was Cletus Kasady,
a mass murderer who eventually becomes the

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.240
supervillain named Carnage.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.660
Carnage is yet another symbiote, an even goopier,
evil-er offspring of the Venom lifeform.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.560
That's right, y'all: Venom's gonna be a mom.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.500
Despite the fact that all the other symbiotes
died in this movie, we know that if Sony decides

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.620
to greenlight a Venom sequel, we've just met
the lead villain.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.460
A lethal protector?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.860
Venom had a pretty hard time keeping his violent
urges in check for the majority of the film.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.640
"So many snacks, so little time"

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.640
The bodega scene at the end is a clear example
of that, since Mrs. Chen sees Eddie's transformation

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.960
and head-eating habits.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.540
So is Eddie going public with his alter ego,
Venom?

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.340
The short answer is, well, maybe!

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.320
We know from the comics, especially the "Lethal
Protector" story from the 1990s, that Brock's

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.900
identity as Venom was known to the residents
of San Francisco though, more as an unstable

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.380
monster than a lovable creep.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.540
The end of the movie seemed to indicate that
the film franchise may be going this route

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.480
as well, at least as far as folks in his San
Francisco neighborhood are concerned.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.540
MCU later?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.340
So is Venom in the MCU?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.060
Sure, Sony and Marvel Studios agreed to share
Spidey for a few MCU movies.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:42.160
But Spider-Man's supporting characters remain
a continuity mystery, since Sony owns their

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.560
movie rights and Marvel doesn't.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.220
There's really no clear answer to this, even
by the movie's end.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.100
No one mentions Tony Stark or SHIELD, so Venom's
connections to the wider Marvel Universe are

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.460
thin to non-existent.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.440
But no one mentions Spider-Man, either.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.000
In the end, Venom seems to take place in its
own little dimension, so all you superfans

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.420
hoping to see Doctor Strange team up with
Venom are probably out of luck.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:04.360
Unless…

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.200
Into the Spider-Verse

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.160
Venom's second post-credits scene teased the
animated Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.300
which teams-up different versions of Spider-Man
from across the multiverse.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.099
And the comics it's based on had more than
just comic book Spideys, including guys like

00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:24.090
the Spider-Man from the 1970s Japanese TV
show, at least a couple cartoon Spider-Men,

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.100
and even the Spider-Man from Capcom's fighting
games.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.160
There was a Spider-Man for every fan.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:31.160
So what's this got to do with Venom?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.760
Well, the Spideys from Sony's previous two
Spider-Man movie franchises Tobey Maguire

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.100
and Andrew Garfield can theoretically connect
up with Tom Holland's Spider-Man.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.959
And while Spider-Man didn't show up in this
movie, Into the Spider-Verse still connects

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:45.940
all of them to Venom.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.940
Venom may never share a milkshake with Drax
the Destroyer, but you can rest easy knowing

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.190
that somewhere in the far reaches of the Spider-Verse,
it just might happen.

